# SSH host keys for the boxes in hosts.conf, pinned so a deploy fails closed on
# an unexpected key instead of trusting it silently.
#
# COPY THIS TO `known_hosts` AND SEED IT YOURSELF. The real file is gitignored:
# it names your servers, which is infrastructure identity and does not belong in
# a public repository.
#
#   ssh-keyscan -H <your-host> >> deploy/ops/known_hosts
#
# Seed it from keys you have ALREADY been deploying to successfully, rather than
# from whatever answers next — the point is to pin what you have historically
# trusted, not to re-trust an unknown.
#
# Refresh a line ONLY when you know why the key changed (a rebuild, a re-image).
# An unexplained change is precisely the case this file exists to catch: stop and
# find out why before you push a release through it.
#
# Format is standard known_hosts, one key per line:
# <host> ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nza...
